    "narrative": "The lineup today for Ghost Ride the WHIP is anchored by **James Wood**, whose 76.27 projection leads the squad as he faces J.T. Ginn. **Wood**\u2019s elite xwOBA of .437 combined with a favorable #1 batting order position makes him our primary offensive engine. Closely trailing him is **Mickey Moniak**, who benefits from a stellar +14% park factor and +19% SP skill boost against Lowder, and **Vinnie Pasquantino**, who faces Canning in a favorable environment that elevates his utility slot value to 72.92. **Tyler Soderstrom** also earns a strong recommendation at 72.71; while his status remains pending, the combination of a high-ceiling park and a +19% skill matchup against the mediocre Zack Littell makes him a foundational piece for today\u2019s production.\n\nWe continue to prioritize stolen base upside, though our aggressive pursuit of efficiency necessitates a few tough calls. **Corbin Carroll** remains a critical start at 69.43, even with a slight drag from a tough matchup against May. The most difficult benching decision was **Austin Riley**, whose 52.16 score narrowly missed the cut behind **Isaac Paredes** and **Josh Naylor**. While **Riley** offers pop, the optimizer favored **Paredes** due to his projected #3 spot in the order and a +17% SP skill advantage against Rogers. We are also monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" designations, most notably for **Jose Caballero** and **Zach McKinstry**; while their scores are currently marginal, any shift in the batting order could necessitate a late swap to optimize our limited game caps. Caution is advised for **Gabriel Moreno** and **Corbin Carroll** against the challenging May, though their current output projections still warrant active status in a 5x5 format that demands consistent daily contributions.",
